{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Torsion.weak_equiv_invariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Torsion.weak_equiv_invariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.weak_equiv_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.weak_equiv_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/weak_equiv_invariance.lean#L36-L50","doc":"**Content statement** (from manuscript):\n\nLet $(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)$ be a quantum observable universe and let\n$\\{A_n\\}_{n \\geq 0}$ be its recursive brane tower with cosimplicial\ncrossed groupoid structure\n([cosimplicial crossed groupoid](#prop:cosimplicial-crossed-groupoid)); let $q$ denote the substrate parameter.  Let\n$\\tau \\colon \\mathcal{A}_\\infty \\to \\mathbb{C}$ be the\n([vacuum state](#prop:vacuum-state)).  A *weak equivalence* between\nbrane levels $n$ and $m$ is a zigzag of coface and codegeneracy maps\n\n    The Lean encoding below states the manuscript claim over a context class and discharges it from the class's fields (§3b-conditional). The declaration type-checks as a complete term; the substantive mathematical content is carried by the context-class axioms, and a full derivation from substrate primitives remains pending. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:weak-equiv-invariance","label":"prop:weak-equiv-invariance","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/weak-equiv-invariance.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.impl_weak_equiv_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.impl_weak_equiv_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/weak_equiv_invariance.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Manuscript identity: vacuum state is invariant under weak\nequivalence between brane levels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.invariance_active","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.invariance_active","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/weak_equiv_invariance.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Hypothesis that weak equivalence invariance is active. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.weak_equiv_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.weak_equiv_invariant","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/weak_equiv_invariance.lean#L27-L27","doc":"Proposition: the weak equivalence invariance holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.weak_equiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.weak_equiv","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/weak_equiv_invariance.lean#L25-L25","doc":"Predicate: levels `n` and `m` are connected by a weak\nequivalence (zigzag of coface/codegeneracy maps). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.τ_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.τ_value","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/weak_equiv_invariance.lean#L22-L22","doc":"Vacuum-state evaluation `τ : 𝒜_∞ → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.q","kind":"def","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/weak_equiv_invariance.lean#L20-L20","doc":"The substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/weak_equiv_invariance.lean#L18-L18","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.WeakEquivInvarianceContext","kind":"class","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/weak_equiv_invariance.lean#L15-L34","doc":"Abstract context for the `weak_equiv_invariance` claim — manuscript-named\ntyped fields below; the `holds` field carries the `Prop`-valued\nclaim of the lemma. ","signatureChunk":0}]}